{
  "id": "27886_oshisemaru",
  "headword": "押し迫る",
  "reading": "おしせまる",
  "romaji": "oshisemaru",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (godan)",
  "gloss": "to be imminent; to draw near; to press in",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to be imminent; to draw near; to press close",
      "explanation": "Of a deadline, the year's end, or an event: to be close at hand and pressing. Conveys a sense of mounting urgency as the time approaches."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "27886_oshisemaru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{年末|ねんまつ}が{押|お}し{迫|せま}ってきた。",
      "english": "The end of the year is fast approaching.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "27886_oshisemaru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{締|し}め{切|き}りが{押|お}し{迫|せま}っている。",
      "english": "The deadline is looming.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "27886_oshisemaru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{試験|しけん}が{押|お}し{迫|せま}り、{毎晩|まいばん}{遅|おそ}くまで{勉強|べんきょう}している。",
      "english": "With the exam fast approaching, I study late every night.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY:\n- Intransitive ({自動詞|じどうし}); the approaching thing is the subject (が).\n\nASPECT (ている):\n- Most often used in the ている / てくる forms ({押|お}し{迫|せま}っている, {押|お}し{迫|せま}ってきた) to express that the time is now pressing.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {年末|ねんまつ}が{押|お}し{迫|せま}る: the year-end is drawing near\n- {締|し}め{切|き}りが{押|お}し{迫|せま}る: the deadline is looming\n- {期限|きげん}が{押|お}し{迫|せま}る: the time limit is approaching",
